# expect-error: line 8: error[undefined]: unknown exception class `OverflowErroandr` — did you mean `OverflowError`?
# A capitalised name in `catch` is an exception class: an unknown one is a
# Lam error (found by lamfuzz: it failed in go build with "undefined").
# A lowercase name is still a catch-all binding.
func main() {
    try {
        print(1)
    } catch OverflowErroandr {
        print("x")
    }
    try {
        print(2)
    } catch e {
        print(e)
    }
}
